   - without an opt-in owner, navigation closes dialogs as before.

2. An active opt-in may preserve dialogs only across navigation that remains
   on the same canonical application path.
   - query changes are same-page;
   - fragment changes are adjudicated explicitly;
   - navigation to another path closes dialogs.

3. Multiple owners are supported safely.
   - reference-counted or otherwise exact ownership;
   - disposing one owner cannot disable another;
   - disposal is idempotent;
   - no static/global process state.

